# Without this, a contributor's local core.autocrlf setting decides line
# endings on checkout - on Windows with autocrlf=true (a common default),
# a *.sh file would check out with CRLF and immediately break when run
# via bash (`$'\r': command not found`, or a bad-interpreter error).
# Force the correct ending per file type regardless of whose machine
# clones this repo.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
